\listaudiodev prints the available audio devices to the
traceback area, each with its ID number.
It takes no arguments:

\listaudiodev

The output looks like this:

    0: HDA Intel PCH: ALC257 Analog (hw:0,0)
    1: ...

The ID numbers are the ones used by \setaudiodev,
\setinaudiodev and \setoutaudiodev.
